{"id": "EUVD-2026-97687", "enisaUuid": "0e1753af-a9fa-3334-9736-6530363f0621", "description": "FreeRDP from 3.0.0 before 3.32.0 contains an incorrect permission assignment vulnerability that allows local users to read private keys written by crypto_write_pem without owner-only permissions. Attackers on multi-user Unix hosts can enumerate the shared temporary directory during soft-smartcard logon to read the world-readable PKINIT private-key copy.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T16:04:18", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T15:26:52", "baseScore": 4.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:P/PR:L/UI:P/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP/security/advisories/GHSA-q9p9-j22r-577p", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/freerdp-3.0.0-before-3.32.0-insecure-permissions-on-soft-smartcard-private-key-file"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109243", "GHSA-p86r-cw4x-6prq"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.09, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "4093849d-d2f8-3d28-9ae6-da317287ef7e", "product": {"name": "FreeRDP", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}, "product_version": "3.0.0 <3.32.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "014e8fae-ee48-3be6-bc6d-124decc72236", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}], "isExploited": false}